1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roars]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
[narrator] Strange beasts and monsters...

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
vast riches, hidden treasures...

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
evil haunts, uncharted frontiers...

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The mysterious unknown...

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
the people who are captivated
by the magic in those words...

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,000
are called...

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Hunters.

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,000
[theme music plays]

10
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,000
-[Satotz] Gon!
-[Gon] Where is everybody?

11
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,000
[Satotz] You must lie down.
You need to rest.

12
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
[footsteps continue]

13
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
[doors clap]

14
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:09,000
SOME X BROTHER X TROUBLE

15
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,000
[music plays]

16
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
[narrator] After learning the reason
for Killua’s disqualification,

17
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Gon was furious with Gittarrackur
or rather, with Killua's brother, Illumi.

18
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Apologize to Killua!

19
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Sorry? But what for?

20
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
-You don't know what you did wrong?
-[Illumi] No.

21
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
You’re not qualified
to be his big brother.

22
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,000
I didn’t know I had to qualify.

23
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
[all gasp]

24
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Friends don’t have to, either.
He gets to choose!

25
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
[Illumi] This boy...

26
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:37,000
[Gon] Don't even bother apologizing.
Just take me to see Killua.

27
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,000
And what will you do?

28
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,000
[Gon] It's obvious!

29
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
I'll bring him back!

30
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
From the sound of it, you must think
I kidnapped my little brother.

31
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:52,000
But he walked out of here
of his own free will.

32
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
He left, but not by free will.

33
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:01,000
You guys were manipulating him.
That's the same thing as kidnapping!

34
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:14,000
We were just discussing
that very subject, Gon.

35
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,000
In fact, Kurapika and Leorio have both
lodged complaints.

36
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:23,000
The committee has been reviewing
the fairness of Killua's disqualification.

37
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:28,000
You saw it yourself. Both during and since
his match with the man called Gitarrackur,

38
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Killua behaved strangely.

39
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:33,000
I believe that there is only reason
that Killua committed murder.

40
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,000
He was hypnotized.

41
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
It’s generally considered impossible
to use hypnosis

42
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
to direct someone to do such a thing,

43
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:46,000
however, assassins raised Killua
and murder was commonplace,

44
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:49,000
so it's natural that he would lack
the proper ethical restraint.

45
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:55,000
It's worth noting that the attack happened
during my match with Bodoro.

46
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:01,000
So, it's possible Killua intended
to aid my cause.

47
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Which means if you're going to disqualify
anyone, it should be me!

48
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Whatever the case, it's obvious
that Killua was not in full control

49
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,000
of his actions at the time.

50
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Thus, he should not
have been disqualified!

51
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:22,000
That is nothing more than speculation.
There's no concrete proof.

52
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,000
From what we saw,
there were no clear indications

53
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,000
he was ordered to commit murder.

54
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:33,000
And regarding the hypnotism, I would have
to question that claim, as well.

55
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
I will agree that the incident occurred

56
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:41,000
once the battle between Leorio
and Bodoro had gotten underway.

57
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:46,000
At that point, both fighters were evenly
matched, all things considered.

58
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
While Bodoro certainly had
more experience,

59
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
it was clear that Leorio
had the definite edge

60
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
when it came to raw ability in combat.

61
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Given that it was a fair fight,
there was no need for Killua to interfere.

62
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,000
[scoffs]

63
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,000
And speaking of weird things happening...

64
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:07,000
why don't we talk about
when you fought with Hisoka?

65
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Mind telling us what it was
he said to you?

66
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:15,000
Neither of you looked tired.

67
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
But Hisoka whispered something to you,
then surrendered.

68
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,000
Weird, right?

69
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,000
I'd understand if he whispered something
and you surrendered,

70
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:29,000
like with Hanzo and me,
or Bodoro and Hisoka.

71
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
We were under a lot of pressure.

72
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Instead, the opposite happened,

73
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:39,000
which makes me wonder if the two of you
struck some sort of bargain.

74
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:43,000
If you want to talk about things
that don't make sense,

75
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,000
then your victory fit the bill perfectly.

76
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:53,000
You don’t have anything to hide, right?
So what did he say? Enlighten us.

77
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
I have no such obligation.

78
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Maybe you don't,
but I think you owe it to us.

79
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,000
I don't.

80
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,000
You may find my victory suspect,

81
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:08,000
but I would say the same
of victory by default.

82
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,000
[growls] What?

83
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,000
[Gon] This is pointless.

84
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,000
[Hanzo] Come on.

85
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Let's just get this over with
so we can all go home.

86
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,000
Look here, pal.

87
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
This is completely pointless!

88
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Why argue about whether somebody
should have passed?

89
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:42,000
If you’re not satisfied that you made it,
you can keep working until you are.

90
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:47,000
If Killua wants to retake the Hunter Exam,
then I know he'll pass!

91
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:51,000
He didn't this time, and it is what it is.

92
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:56,000
But still, if you've been forcing Killua
to murder people

93
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
against his will, this whole time...

94
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,000
I will never forgive you.

95
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Never forgive me?

96
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,000
So, what will you do?

97
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:13,000
I won't do anything.
But after I go rescue Killua,

98
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,000
I'll never let you see him again!

99
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Hmm...

100
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,000
[clears throat]

101
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,000
Alright, gentlemen. Let's continue.

102
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
Gon's absolutely right.

103
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:41,000
It’s up to each of you to decide
whether you’re worthy of your license.

104
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:45,000
Now, you’re all perfectly welcome
to complain about the results

105
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:48,000
as much as you like,
but our minds are made up.

106
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:53,000
Killua has been disqualified
from this year's Hunter Exam,

107
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,000
while the rest of you have passed.

108
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Alright then, I shall continue
with the orientation.

109
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Now, the cards that we’ve passed out
are your Hunter licenses.

110
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:17,000
This card will allow you
to enter 90 percent of the countries

111
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,000
that limit immigration,
as well as grant you access

112
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:24,000
to 75 percent of restricted areas
in the world.

113
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Amazing.

114
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:31,000
You may use 95 percent of public
facilities at absolutely no cost,

115
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,000
and banks will treat you
as if you were a top-rated company.

116
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:40,000
You can sell it for enough money
to last seven lifetimes,

117
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
or you can keep it for a life
of guaranteed comfort.

118
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Please be very careful. You wouldn’t
want it to be misplaced or stolen.

119
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,000
You won't get a replacement.

120
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:58,000
According to our estimates,
as many as one in five Hunters

121
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:02,000
somehow manage to lose their card
within a year of receiving it.

122
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Your very first challenge
as a licensed Hunter

123
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,000
is to protect your card at all costs.

124
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,000
From here on out, it's your show.

125
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Believe in yourselves, and keep working
to make your dreams come true.

126
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:23,000
Well, then we can now certify
all seven applicants present

127
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,000
as licensed Hunters.

128
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:36,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

129
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:41,000
LICENSE

130
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
[Gon] Gittarackur.

131
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,000
I want you to tell me where Killua is.

132
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,000
You're really going after him?

133
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:05,000
-I think that's a bad idea.
-Who cares what you think?

134
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,000
Killua is my friend.
I'll get him back, I swear.

135
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:14,000
And do they feel the same way?

136
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:16,000
You bet we do.

137
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:26,000
Fine, then. I doubt you'll be able
to get there, anyway.

138
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:29,000
I'm sure Kil just went back home.

139
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,000
Where's that?

140
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
On Kukuroo Mountain.

141
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,000
You can find our family's house
at the summit.

142
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,000
[Leorio] Kukuroo Mountain?

143
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
[Gon] We got it. Thanks a lot.

144
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,000
[Hisoka] Was that wise?

145
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:49,000
Giving up your base of operations
like that?

146
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:52,000
Sure, it isn't a secret.

147
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:55,000
The locals all know where we live.

148
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Our worlds are drastically different,

149
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,000
a fact that I'm sure they'll all come
to realize once they arrive.

150
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:05,000
-Hmm.
-Oh, this?

151
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,000
Yeah, it's broken.

152
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,000
[Hisoka] Hmm...

153
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,000
He is interesting.

154
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:18,000
I can understand your concern
for his future.

155
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Uh-huh.

156
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:27,000
However, that makes him
all the more dangerous.

157
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,000
I'd like to deal with that as soon as...

158
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Gon is mine. Do not forget that.

159
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:41,000
Leave him be or suffer the consequences.

160
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:43,000
I'm aware of that.

161
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:47,000
I haven't known you long,
but I know your tastes.

162
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
So, Hisoka...

163
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,000
what are you going to do now?

164
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Wait patiently...

165
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,000
[shudders]

166
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,000
until the fruit becomes ripe enough
for me to pluck.

167
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:10,000
[Leorio] Kukuroo Mountain, huh?
Never heard of it.

168
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,000
Do you know where it is, Kurapika?

169
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,000
-Hey, Kurapika!
-Huh?

170
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Oh, what's that?

171
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Pay attention!
Illumi mentioned Kukuroo Mountain.

172
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,000
Do you have any idea where it is?

173
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:29,000
No, I'm afraid I don't,
but we can just go look it up online.

174
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,000
Hey!

175
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:35,000
Oh! Hey, Hanzo!

176
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,000
[Hanzo] I'm heading home.

177
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:41,000
We all went through a lot in a short time
but I had a lot of fun.

178
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,000
[Gon] Yeah, me too.

179
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:45,000
If you ever visit my country,
just let me know.

180
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:48,000
I’ll give you a real tour,
no tourist traps!

181
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Later!

182
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,000
Bye! See you!

183
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,000
CLOUD HIDDEN NINJA HANZO

184
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:02,000
That certainly is one big,
self-assured ninja!

185
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,000
-[Pokkle] Hey.
-[all] Huh?

186
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:09,000
I’m really sorry about getting
so worked up back there.

187
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Please, I was no better.
I hope you’ll forgive me.

188
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:18,000
No, I only got mad because deep down,
I knew you were right.

189
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:22,000
I was just taking out my frustration
at winning by default.

190
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,000
But I'm over that.

191
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:28,000
I passed, so I might as well
make the best of it, right?

192
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:32,000
The question is what am I gonna do next?

193
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,000
[Kurapika] Yes, you're right.

194
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:38,000
I’ve decided that I’ll travel the world,
discover new species

195
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:42,000
and as a licensed Exotic Game Hunter,
learn everything I can.

196
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:46,000
-Exotic Game Hunter?
-Oh, hey, what's that thing?

197
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
[Pokkle] What, this?

198
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:50,000
You use it to find
all kinds of information.

199
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:54,000
Is there anything you wanna know?
I can look it up for you.

200
00:14:56,000 --> 00:15:00,000
Oh, there is! Think you can look up
a Hunter named Ging? Ging Freecss.

201
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:04,000
[Pokkle] Sure, hold on just a second.

202
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,000
What's Satotz doing?

203
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,000
[Pokkle] I'm curious.
So, who is this Ging guy, anyway?

204
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:17,000
[Gon] Huh?

205
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:22,000
‘Cause everything that’s related to him
is behind a tight security system.

206
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,000
You need a whole bunch of codes
to access it.

207
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:28,000
I think he must have friends
on the national level.

208
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,000
Really? Forget it, then.

209
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:36,000
Did you hear that? It sounds like your dad
is someone really special.

210
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,000
[Gon chuckles]

211
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:41,000
[Pokkle] Okay, let me know
if anything comes up.

212
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:43,000
This is my e-mail address.

213
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,000
-See you around!
-Bye, Pokkle!

214
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:53,000
We should have asked him
to look up Kukuroo Mountain.

215
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,000
Yeah, I guess you're right.

216
00:15:55,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Well, we are all Hunters now.
Chairman Netero made that much clear.

217
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:04,000
And it’s probably not the best idea to let
other Hunters know what you’re doing.

218
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,000
-Better to look it up ourselves.
-[all chuckle]

219
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,000
[Satotz] Gon.

220
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,000
Mr. Satotz!

221
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,000
It appears that you forgot something.

222
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Oh, that's right. Thanks a lot!

223
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,000
Also, do you have a brief moment?

224
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,000
-We'll be waiting for you in the lobby.
-[Gon] Okay!

225
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:39,000
Forgive me, I couldn't help
but overhear your conversation.

226
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:44,000
As it happens, I specialize
in ancient ruins,

227
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,000
restoration and preservation.

228
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:50,000
At first, I was fixated on the glory
of new discoveries.

229
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:56,000
But after watching a certain Hunter,
I became quite ashamed of myself.

230
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:04,000
That Hunter of which I speak
would discover ruins,

231
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:07,000
then spend his own money
to completely restore them.

232
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:11,000
He took steps to preserve the sites
for future generations,

233
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:16,000
ensuring that people from every walk
of life would be able to enjoy them.

234
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
His dedication was impressive.

235
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:23,000
I'd say more impressive than the ruins
themselves.

236
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:27,000
His work was documented in manuals,

237
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:31,000
manuals which are now used
in restorations throughout the world.

238
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:35,000
The name of this Hunter, Gon...

239
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:40,000
is none other than Ging Freecss,
the man whom you were just asking about.

240
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,000
[gasps]

241
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:50,000
I wanted so desperately to meet him,
I did a bit of investigating, myself.

242
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:54,000
However, the man is an enigma,

243
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:57,000
and I was never able
to unearth a single thing about him.

244
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,000
Really? That figures.

245
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:04,000
My goal is to become a Hunter,
just like him.

246
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:09,000
And my dream is to thank him
in person, one day.

247
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:11,000
Mm.

248
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,000
That's all I had to say.

249
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
My apologies for interrupting you.

250
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:22,000
It's fine.
Thanks for everything, Mr. Satotz.

251
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,000
-Well, bye!
-Oh, and Gon.

252
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:27,000
Hmm?

253
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:32,000
It's nothing.
Just take care of yourself.

254
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:37,000
Yeah! You do the same.
Goodbye!

255
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:49,000
-First, let's look up Kukuroo Mountain.
-Right.

256
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Kukuroo Mountain.
There. Here it is.

257
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:59,000
"Kukuroo Mountain, in the Dentora Region
of the Republic of Padokea

258
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
is 3,722 meters high."

259
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:04,000
The Republic of Padokea?

260
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,000
Never heard of the place.
So, where is it?

261
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,000
Hold on. I'll bring up a map.

262
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,000
This is the Republic of Padokea.

263
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:18,000
It appears to be a stable country,
so we should be fine.

264
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,000
This country's open to tourists.

265
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,000
That's where Killua is?

266
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:27,000
It'll take three days to reach by airship.
When do you think we should leave?

267
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:30,000
-Today! Right now!
-All right! I'm with Gon.

268
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,000
Got it. I'll order the tickets, then.

269
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:42,000
TAXI

270
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:45,000
What's going on?
Feels like we've been stuck here forever.

271
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:48,000
This is bad. At this rate, we'll be late
for our flight.

272
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,000
[Leorio] Hey, pops! Do something!

273
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:56,000
[driver] Nothing I can do about traffic.
And it's the only road.

274
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,000
In that case...

275
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
[theme music playing]

276
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:08,000
[Gon] Yay!

277
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Hey, Gon! Do you realize
how far away the airport is?

278
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Sure! But I want to go rescue Killua,

279
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:25,000
and I didn't want to wait around
another second!

280
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:29,000
-[Kurapika chuckles]
-Fine, you win.

281
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:36,000
[chuckles] Running like this
kind of reminds me of the Hunter Exam.

282
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,000
[Gon] I know, right!

283
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:43,000
This is a heck of a lot easier
than the Hunter Exam was!

284
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,000
[Leorio] Oh, yeah.

285
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,000
You got that right.

286
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:55,000
[Gon] All right!
Race you guys to the airport!

287
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:01,000
Ready, set, go!

288
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:06,000
[narrator] Gon and his friends set off
for the Republic of Padokea.

289
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:12,000
Their destination is Kukuroo Mountain,
where they hope to find Killua's home.

290
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,000
[Menchi] Satotz.

291
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:26,000
[Satotz] Oh, Menchi and Buhara.

292
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:30,000
Is it just me or was that
a really close call?

293
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:34,000
[Satotz] [chuckles] You saw that, did you?

294
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:39,000
That boy's a mystery.
I feel most compelled to help him.

295
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:44,000
I almost nearly let it slip that...

296
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:51,000
the real Hunter Exam isn't over
just yet.

297
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:00,000
[theme music plays]

298
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:25,000
[Gon] Next time,
"A Dangerous Watchdog."

299
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
-[Gon] Doggy, go, fetch!
-[Leorio] That's it.

300
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:30,000
-[Gon] Doggie, roll over!
-[Leorio] Oh, yeah!
